{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Behold, these were, etc., through the matter of Bilaam.</b> One needs to know the intent of His saying <b>Behold, these were</b>; further, why did He lengthen to say ״through the matter of Bilaam, etc., concerning the matter of Peor״? And the matter will be explained further regarding why Pinchas and the righteous of the Most High erred, who went along with him in this matter." "<b>Indeed</b>, Pinchas and the men of the army judged and acquitted them, for the reason that women are subject to their husbands and to their fathers, and they are coerced. But our master Moses our teacher, peace be upon him, perceived that for this reason they had spared them, and he came with a claim that could be heard and said: Granted, if they had done only the act of harlotry that came upon them by command of their elders, one could judge them favorably; but they did on their own another act that their elders had not commanded them, namely the act of Peor, concerning which our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Numbers Rabbah 20:23) that they would bring before them the image of Peor and say to them: Bow down to this and you will be obeyed by Him. It turns out that a stumbling block of idolatrous worship came from them. And this is what He said <b>Behold, these were</b> — meaning, of themselves they were a cause for the children of Israel. <b>Through the matter of Bilaam</b>, etc. — meaning, by means of the cause of Bilaam's counsel, when he counseled them to expose their daughters to harlotry. And you will find that our Rabbis of blessed memory did not say that Bilaam spoke of anything but the matter of harlotry, as they said (ibid.): their Elohim hates lewdness, etc. And they were a cause to bring treason against HaShem concerning the matter of Peor, for the women did not want to comply with them unless they bowed down to Peor. <b>And the plague was among the congregation of HaShem</b> — meaning, because of idolatrous worship and not because of harlotry; and who caused the idolatrous worship — these women. And He says ״And now,״ etc. — meaning, let them confess the error and let them kill all, etc."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:16:25.276796760Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}